-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/assassination-of-archduke-franz-ferdinand.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Assassination of Archduke Franz Ferdinand</span><span class="enc-type">Event</span><span class="enc-snip">The assassination of Archduke Franz Ferdinand, heir to the Austro-Hungarian throne, took place in Sarajevo in 1914.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/assassination-of-julius-caesar"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/assassination-of-julius-caesar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Assassination of Julius Caesar</span><span class="enc-type">Event</span><span class="enc-snip">The assassination of Julius Caesar was the killing of the Roman dictator by a group of senators in Rome in 44 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/assassination-of-nader-shah"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/assassination-of-nader-shah.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Assassination of Nader Shah</span><span class="enc-type">Event</span><span class="enc-snip">The assassination of Nader Shah was the killing of the founder of the Afsharid Empire by his own officers in 1747.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/assassination-of-rulers"><span class="enc-name">Assassination of rulers</span><span class="enc-type">Historical factor</span><span class="enc-snip">The assassination of rulers is a recurring pattern in which kings, emperors or caliphs are murdered by rivals, courtiers, soldiers or conspirators.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/assassination-of-uthman"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/assassination-of-uthman.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Assassination of Uthman</span><span class="enc-type">Event</span><span class="enc-snip">The a