a was the sack of the Elamite capital by the army of Ashurbanipal in 646 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/assyrian-empire.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Assyrian Empire</span><span class="enc-type">State</span><span class="enc-snip">The Assyrian Empire was a Mesopotamian state centred on Assur and Nineveh on the upper Tigris.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/asta-gudbrandsdatter"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/asta-gudbrandsdatter.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Åsta Gudbrandsdatter</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Åsta Gudbrandsdatter was a Norwegian noblewoman of the late 10th and early 11th centuries, according to the sagas.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/astana"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/astana.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Astana</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Astana is the capital of Kazakhstan, on the Ishim River in the north of the country.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/astana-cemetery"><span class="enc-name">Astana Cemetery</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Astana Cemetery is an ancient burial ground near the ruins of Gaochang, east of Turpan in Xinjiang, China.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/astana-gede"><span class="enc-name">Astana Gede</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Astana Gede is a sacred site at Kawali in Ciamis Regency, West Java, Indonesia, associated with the Sundanese kingdom of Galuh.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/astara"><span class="enc-name">Astara</span><span class="enc-ty